---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/post.css';
---

<Base title="Ethan Fang, Tennis Coach" description="Coaching players in the East Bay.">
  <article class="post">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">&#8592; back</a>

    <header class="post__header">
      <h1 class="post__title">Tennis</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="post__body">
      <p>
        I started playing tennis at the age of 7, and fell in love with the game. I competed in junior tennis at the highest level: reaching top 20 ranking in Northern California,
        playing several of the super national L1s, representing Team NorCal at Zonals, and reaching a peak UTR of 10. Along the way, I picked up partial sponsorships from Babolat, Solinco, and Adidas.
        I also played high school tennis, only losing 3 matches across 4 years in dual match play. I earned 2nd place at NCS individuals my senior year with a good friend.
      </p>
      <p>
        As my junior career winded down, I began coaching privately, working with students who ranged from complete beginners to future D1-3 players. 
      </p>
      <p>
        In college, I chose to focus on acadeics. I attended Case Western, and wanted to serve my tennis community. I helped grow club tennis from 20 members to 120 and 
        secured a team sponsorship with Solinco. We set record practice attendances, and sign-ups would fill up in under 9 seconds whenever they were released every week.
        I cofounded the Cleveland Classic Club Tennis tournament with Cleveland State University in 2023, which has run annually for 3 consecutive years and allowed hundreds
        of club players across the country to come out and compete in Cleveland. I played mostly recreationally in college, but still competed in club tournaments with friends.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nowadays, I like to help out in my community through coaching junior players in the East Bay. I do privates and 1 on 1 hitting sessions, 
        and focus on a combination of technique and matchplay mentality. Please reach out if interested.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
